Operator troubleshooting surface on CLI and MCP with parity: session search | timeline | diff | dump | export | show --turns | ingest | prune.

WHY (measured): `ddflow session --help` lists only start, prompt, note, adopt-orphans, end, list, show (surfaces/declared/records.py:348-432, commands/viewers_sessions.py). `session show` prints prompts and notes only; there is no timeline, no diff of two sessions, no dump of a whole session or an agent's history, no export of a session's context for a bug report. MCP has ddflow_session_start/prompt/note/end, ddflow_prompts (which is about prompt TEMPLATES), ddflow_history (events, not turns); no MCP way to read a session. Usability bug found while probing: `session list` prints truncated ids (s20261008T152231-17349) but `session show` rejects them ('no session ...; did you mean s20261008T152231-1734981') - list must print full ids or show must accept a unique prefix (file as a bug with a regression test when this task starts).

COMMANDS (declared once in the command registry, ddflow/surfaces/declared, so CLI and MCP derive from one declaration; read-only commands get MCP tools in the read tier):
 - session search <query> [--agent --session --role --since --limit --regex --exact] (thin alias of search --source transcripts,sessions with the same output);
 - session timeline <id|--agent U1> [--since --until]: chronological one-line-per-turn view with tool names, gate verdicts and lease events interleaved from the event log;
 - session diff <idA> <idB>: what two sessions did differently: items held, files touched, commands failed, decisions, handoff fields side by side;
 - session dump <id> [--turns a-b --full --format md|json]: everything for the session, redacted with the 'export' profile, stdout or --out;
 - session export <id|--agent> [--out FILE]: a self-contained bundle (handoff + turns + pointers) for a bug report, redacted with the 'upstream' profile;
 - session show <id> --turns a-b, session ingest, session prune --dry-run.
 MCP: ddflow_session_search / _timeline / _diff / _dump (size-capped output, cursor for more), same help text and exit semantics (0/1/2/3).

PIN/TEST: CLI<->MCP parity test that already exists for declared commands extended; goldens for existing session list/show; secrets planted in a transcript never appear in dump/export; dump of a 10 MB session honours the cap and says what was cut. EXPECTED SIZE: ~600 lines + tests ~400 (split into search/timeline, diff, dump/export slices if needed).

